  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef's favorite clothing store is holding a clearance sale: for every 222 t-shirts bought, you receive a third one for free!\n\nChef bought and paid for XXX t-shirts from the shop. It is guaranteed that XXX **is even.**\n\nHow many t-shirts did Chef get from the shop in total?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input contains a single even integer XXX, the number of t-shirts Chef paid for.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line one integer: the total number of t-shirts Chef will get from the store.",
    "constraints": [
      "2≤X≤1002 \\leq X \\leq 1002≤X≤100",
      "XXX is even."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "30",
        "output": "45",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef paid for 303030 t-shirts. Every two t-shirts will give Chef one extra free t-shirt, so Chef will get 302=15\\frac{30}{2} = 15230​=15 free t-shirts.\nThe total number of t-shirts is hence 30+15=4530+15 = 4530+15=45."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "88",
        "output": "132",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef paid for 888888 t-shirts. Every two t-shirts will give Chef one extra free t-shirt, so Chef will get 882=44\\frac{88}{2} = 44288​=44 free t-shirts.\nThe total number of t-shirts is hence 88+44=13288+44 = 13288+44=132."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4",
        "output": "6",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef paid for 444 t-shirts. Every two t-shirts will give Chef one extra free t-shirt, so Chef will get 42=2\\frac{4}{2} = 224​=2 free t-shirts.\nThe total number of t-shirts is hence 4+2=64+2 = 64+2=6."
      }
    ]
  },
